    "result_text": "I added a search box to the Clients page that filters the list by name. `bin/e2e` builds the app and the acceptance test passes.\n\n**How it works:** the change is all in one file, `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/clients/clients.ts`.\n- The box (`data-testid=\"client-search\"`) has a visible label and sits above the clients table.\n- Matching ignores upper/lower case and finds the text anywhere in the name, so \"glob\" finds \"Globex\". Spaces at either end are ignored.\n- An empty box shows every client.\n- If nothing matches, the page says \"No clients match your search.\" (`data-testid=\"clients-no-match\"`). The existing \"No clients yet.\" message still shows only when there are no clients at all.\n- No existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.\n\n**Not done: database and server changes.** The task asked for a migration and server changes, but this feature didn't need either. The page already loads every client, so filtering happens in the browser and the search adds no extra server requests. Also, the task said \"OfficeFloor server\", but the server in this repo is Spring Boot. I left both unchanged.\n\nIf the client list grows large enough that loading all of it becomes slow, the next step would be a `?name=` filter on `GET /api/clients`.",
